      bases: { GER: "Rome", UK: "Sicily", USA: "Sicily" },
      _note: "Sicily, the islands and the peninsula as far as the Gothic Line (Emilia and Liguria), with Malta, where the invasion convoys gather. Cassino and the Abruzzo are the two ends of the Gustav Line; Anzio is the beach behind it. Italy has no plan here: it defends its own country by the main rules until the armistice (see diplomacy.json). The Allied phases marked ifLost Sicily keep the landing in Sicily on the table for as long as the island is in enemy hands, and the German phases marked ifLost Sicily are the retreat up the peninsula, which only begins once the island has gone. In 1944 each further step back waits on the ground the same way: the counter-attack at Anzio on a beachhead to attack, the retreat north of Rome on the fall of Cassino, the Gothic Line on the fall of Rome. The British and American plans name their own targets so that the Eighth Army keeps to the Adriatic side and the Fifth to the west.",
      regions: ["Malta", "Sicily", "Calabria", "Apulia", "Naples", "Cassino", "Anzio", "Abruzzo", "Rome", "Marche", "Tuscany", "Emilia", "Liguria", "Sardinia", "Corsica"],
